  "body": "Part of #2238 (frame cost: calculate before and cache). Measured with the frame-cost probe of #2238, release build, fig8.step.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe Geometry tab of an operation with a welded face pick (Source: Selection) calculates these values on each frame, also when no input changed:\n\n| Piece | Function | ms per frame (release) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ui/properties.op.picks.chips` | `geo_page::chips` -> `State::geo_chips`, `camcraft_app::pick::face_origin` for each face chip | 4.68 |\n| `ui/properties.op.picks.align_321` | `camcraft_app::pick::align_321` | 1.98 |\n\nState: 2D Adaptive, one welded face (the face with the most strips), Boundary group open. Debug build: 78 ms for all of `ui/properties.op.picks`.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The chip list (labels, missing flags, face origin targets) and the 3-2-1 result are calculated when the picks or the model change, and read from a cache on other frames.\n- The cache key follows `docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md`: the pick list value, and the `Arc` of the model features.\n- A counter test: a still frame makes zero new calculations.\n- A changed-input test: a new pick gives a new chip list, equal to a fresh calculation.\n- The probe `frame_cost_probe` shows `ui/properties.op.picks` under 1 ms in release for this state.\n- No change to the commands, the picks, the WCS result or the posted G-code.\n",
